The follow-up review confirmed persistent holds are eliminated, but identified two remaining pre-execution gaps: a paused non-atomic image write could look stable, and raw `code:` keys were parsed without checking Linux’s supported range. I’m closing both by validating complete PNG/JPEG/WebP containers before accepting a frame and validating every key’s injectability before any action in the batch runs.
